            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Snap, Google, Robinhood: Trending stocks",
            "description": "<p>Google's (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GOOGL\">GOOGL</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GOOG\">GOOG</a>) multibillion-dollar AI dealmaking spree continues, including a potential partnership with Apple (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL\">AAPL</a>). <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SNAP\">SNAP</a> stock pops on strong earnings, fueling hopes of a rebound. Robinhood (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/HOOD\">HOOD</a>) shares turn red in pre-market. And as Hong Kong surpasses the NYSE and NASDAQ as the world's top listing venue, IPO's of autonomous driving firms Pony AI (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/PONY\">PONY</a>) and WeRide (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WRD\">WRD</a>) nosedive on their debuts.</p>\n<p>For more live coverage of the markets, watch the full episode of <em>Market Sunrise</em> and visit<a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/\"> Yahoo Finance</a>.</p>",
